{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And HaShem called HaShem.</b> I am the Master of mercy before a person sins and after a person sins — thus they explain it in tractate Rosh HaShanah. And it requires study: why does a person need mercy before he sins? And one may say: it is nevertheless so, that he needs mercy because it is revealed and known before the Holy One, blessed be He, that he will eventually sin. According to this, the second Name is among the thirteen attributes, but נוצר חסד לאלפים is counted only as one. And the Rav, Rabbi Nissim, of blessed memory, explained: נוצר חסד לאלפים are two attributes, and the first Name is not counted in the enumeration. And the plain sense of the verse — ויעבור ה' על פניו ויקרא בשם ה' — 'ה' אל רחום' etc.: these attributes you shall call upon before Me when you need mercy." "<b>El.</b> A true judge and a righteous judge — as in עד האלהים יבא דבר שניהם — both of them." "<b>Rachum.</b> That He has mercy on the poor and rescues them." "<b>And chanun.</b> Even to the rich, for everyone who gives a gift is חונן — as in וצדיק חונן ונותן." "<b>Erech appaim.</b> Toward the wicked, for He does not hasten to exact punishment from them." "<b>And abundant lovingkindness.</b> That He multiplies His lovingkindness over the measure of punishment, as our Sages, may their memory be blessed, said: the measure of good exceeds the measure of punishment." "<b>And truth.</b> What I promise — if one does good for people — [will be fulfilled], provided the person does not act negligently with himself so as to sin and cause [the consequence of] the sin."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The reading of the last phrase 'תקראו לפני' is uncertain; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:45.437300851Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}